1
00:00:00,490 --> 00:00:03,719
Have I really fallen for him?

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:04,860
Fallen for So-chan...

3
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:06,370
Sorry.

4
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:07,520
Na-chan.

5
00:00:07,521 --> 00:00:09,449
So... it was just a joke.

6
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:10,300
Of course.
Huh?

7
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:11,640
Huh?

8
00:00:11,641 --> 00:00:13,370
Sota isn't my boyfriend.

9
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,959
Does he think less of me?

10
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,049
Does he think I'm gross?

11
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:18,050
No way.

12
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,930
Sota isn't like that.

13
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:27,600
I want to have a proper talk
with you after the mock exams.

14
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:30,520
I think I'm really going to get dumped.

15
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:32,230
Natsuki?

16
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,040
Huh, talking to yourself?

17
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,130
Sigh...

18
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:48,030
Your Summer, My Storm
(Episode 7)

19
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,560
Crap.

20
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,280
It actually sent.

21
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:54,800
Wait.

22
00:00:54,801 --> 00:00:56,060
What do I do...

23
00:00:57,850 --> 00:00:58,850
Ah...

24
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,460
Ah, unsend, unsend it quickly.

25
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:01,640
(Read)

26
00:01:01,870 --> 00:01:02,870
Ah!

27
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:07,960
Huh?

28
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,620
(Understood)

29
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:12,380
Huh...

30
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:15,129
No way...

31
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:18,560
Making a mistake I'd normally never make.

32
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:21,820
I'm seriously panicking right now.

33
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:23,960
Sigh...

34
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:26,920
What on earth should I do?

35
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:30,170
What on earth should I do?

36
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:33,120
Huh, what's going on?

37
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,199
Did Towako-san find out?

38
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:35,840
No.

39
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,060
She didn't find out, but...

40
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:39,380
Honey.

41
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:42,600
Are you hiding something from me?

42
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:45,370
Don't tell me...

43
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:47,410
You're having an affair?

44
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:49,390
Don't be silly.

45
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,389
How could that possibly be true?

46
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:54,250
You're overreacting. You are
hiding something, aren't you?

47
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:55,906
Do you really have that little faith in me?

48
00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:57,359
The way you're talking...

49
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,180
How am I supposed to believe you?

50
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,270
No way...
Old man.

51
00:02:05,161 --> 00:02:07,129
How are you so bad at lying?

52
00:02:07,130 --> 00:02:08,570
I can't help it...

53
00:02:09,690 --> 00:02:10,690
Fukuo.

54
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:12,680
Tell me what I should do.

55
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:14,279
What do you want me to say...

56
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,280
Sigh...

57
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:19,320
Sigh...

58
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,290
Seriously...

59
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:25,420
I rarely panic like this.

60
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:28,599
I usually use probability and statistics.

61
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,430
To anticipate every possible scenario.

62
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,280
Then I formulate a meticulous plan.

63
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:37,600
And I'm the type of person
who likes to stick to the plan.

64
00:02:39,290 --> 00:02:40,290
So...

65
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,780
No matter how much I
analyze it, I can't find the answer.

66
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:45,499
(You are my light)
Love has no correct solution.

67
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,910
I'm really bad at dealing with it.

68
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:56,030
I think it might have to
do with how I grew up.

69
00:02:59,290 --> 00:03:02,860
My family is quite a prominent
and well-known household in the area.

70
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,719
Oh my, it's Sota.

71
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,959
- Take care.
- Ever since I was little...

72
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,699
I was put on a pedestal as
a young master or a prodigy.

73
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,249
It's Kobayakawa Sota.

74
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:12,029
He's smart and handsome.

75
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:13,039
And he's so ambitious.

76
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,379
- So cool.
- But people only paid attention to me...

77
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:18,140
Just because I was "the son
of the Kobayakawa family."

78
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:21,720
They didn't see me as a romantic interest.

79
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,710
After moving to Tokyo for college...

80
00:03:26,010 --> 00:03:27,770
No one paid special
attention to me anymore.

81
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,460
That sense of liberation
made me feel so at ease.

82
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:34,009
I never thought about
dating like my friends did.

83
00:03:34,010 --> 00:03:36,090
Nor did I feel like I absolutely had to.

84
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:42,720
Oh...

85
00:03:43,770 --> 00:03:46,300
Now, I live every day
freely and comfortably.

86
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,840
And with absolutely no immunity to love...

87
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:56,090
Have I really fallen for him?

88
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:58,170
Fallen for So-chan...

89
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:01,200
Having Na-chan confess
his feelings to me...

90
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:06,430
Made me panic and completely lose control.

91
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:07,950
Which is only natural.

92
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:12,089
Thanks for waiting.

93
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:13,470
Crab and cabbage fried rice.

94
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:16,830
I couldn't answer anything...

95
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,160
What about Natsuki?

96
00:04:19,230 --> 00:04:20,429
He looks like he aced it.

97
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:21,629
That's amazing.

98
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:23,389
The tutoring really paid off.

99
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:23,920
Huh?

100
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,280
Ah, the mock exams?

101
00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:26,430
Ah...

102
00:04:26,670 --> 00:04:27,600
Yeah, it went okay.

103
00:04:27,601 --> 00:04:28,799
Damn it.

104
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,480
Ah.

105
00:04:29,481 --> 00:04:32,299
Someone come be my tutor.

106
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:32,920
How about me?
Huh, really?

107
00:04:33,641 --> 00:04:34,779
I'd be a better choice, right?

108
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:35,530
I'd be better.

109
00:04:35,531 --> 00:04:36,699
- Huh?
- I'd be better.

110
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:37,280
Huh?

111
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:40,909
Sorry, I sent that last message by mistake.

112
00:04:40,910 --> 00:04:41,910
Don't worry about it.

113
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:44,810
Did I reply wrong again?

114
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:48,430
It seems that on my own...

115
00:04:48,777 --> 00:04:51,776
I can't find the right answer at all.

116
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:52,800
(Rio)

117
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:57,330
I see.

118
00:04:57,830 --> 00:04:59,230
Na-chan told you...

119
00:04:59,690 --> 00:05:00,690
Yeah.

120
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:04,649
I was just wanting to
hear your thoughts, Sota.

121
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:06,090
And then you happened to contact me.

122
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:09,860
Were you shocked?

123
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:12,720
Yeah...

124
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:14,740
To be honest...

125
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:17,320
I was really panicking a bit.

126
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:19,460
That makes sense.

127
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,720
I always thought...

128
00:05:24,410 --> 00:05:28,490
I was understanding of diversity
and minority groups.

129
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:32,540
I never thought there was
anything weird or wrong about it.

130
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,506
Even though I don't have anyone
like that around me right now...

131
00:05:35,530 --> 00:05:37,360
I always felt I'd definitely be accepting.

132
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,120
But when it actually happens to you...

133
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,680
You still don't know what to do?

134
00:05:47,390 --> 00:05:48,680
It's a bit embarrassing...

135
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:53,370
But I really don't know how to face it.

136
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:55,850
And I don't know what to do.

137
00:05:55,851 --> 00:05:57,310
It's not embarrassing at all.

138
00:05:57,870 --> 00:06:00,399
I just wish I could be more positive...

139
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,250
And accept it naturally.

140
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,640
Yeah.

141
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,000
But isn't that because...

142
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,270
Society hasn't reached that point yet?

143
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:11,960
Is that it...?

144
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:12,830
Yeah.

145
00:06:13,150 --> 00:06:14,700
You see, my parents are like that too.

146
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,440
Especially my dad.

147
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,909
If I told him about two guys dating...

148
00:06:18,910 --> 00:06:21,790
He'd probably say something rude
like, "What a disgrace."

149
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:31,930
What did Sota say?

150
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,180
He said sorry...

151
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:37,620
Sigh...

152
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,560
Crap...

153
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:48,650
Na-chan...

154
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,160
Yeah.

155
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:51,990
All this time...

156
00:06:52,590 --> 00:06:53,590
Um...

157
00:06:54,270 --> 00:06:56,940
He's only ever dated girls, right?

158
00:06:58,110 --> 00:06:58,670
Yeah.

159
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,710
He's only ever been with girls.

160
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,220
But that kid...

161
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:08,560
Has never truly liked anyone.

162
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:10,470
Is that so?

163
00:07:12,570 --> 00:07:13,900
Natsuki...

164
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:17,420
Even though it's weird for
me as his sister to say this...

165
00:07:17,930 --> 00:07:20,800
He is gentle and pretty good-looking.

166
00:07:21,017 --> 00:07:23,766
He's been super
popular since he was little.

167
00:07:23,790 --> 00:07:24,830
Hey, Na-chan.

168
00:07:26,090 --> 00:07:27,999
Na-chan is mine, right?

169
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,339
He's mine.

170
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:30,679
He's obviously mine.

171
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,059
He's mine!

172
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:32,960
He's obviously mine!

173
00:07:32,961 --> 00:07:34,700
Don't fight.

174
00:07:35,290 --> 00:07:37,070
So, Na-chan, who do you like?

175
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,159
Uh...

176
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,800
That kid's gentleness...

177
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,040
Is basically just indecisiveness.

178
00:07:46,410 --> 00:07:47,410
Thank you.

179
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:51,130
Are you okay?

180
00:07:51,131 --> 00:07:52,300
I'm fine.

181
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:56,140
Should I say he's just naturally
easy to fall for?

182
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:58,420
I like you.

183
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:00,700
Thank you.
Huh?

184
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:02,830
Will you go out with me?

185
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:04,290
Huh?

186
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:06,260
Ah.

187
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:07,130
Yeah.
Really?

188
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:09,070
Yeah.
Let's go out.

189
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:10,480
I'm so happy!

190
00:08:10,481 --> 00:08:11,789
Whenever someone confesses to him...

191
00:08:11,790 --> 00:08:13,670
He ends up dating them
because he can't say no.

192
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,720
But once they start dating...

193
00:08:16,410 --> 00:08:18,160
He tries hard to be a good boyfriend.

194
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,430
He tries hard to make himself like them.

195
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:21,940
But...

196
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,980
Falling for someone isn't exactly
something you can force, right?

197
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:27,560
Yeah.

198
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:29,260
That feeling...

199
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:31,640
The other person can actually sense it.

200
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:34,029
That's why every time,

201
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:35,350
he always ends up getting dumped.

202
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,080
I see...

203
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:39,450
I'm the same way, so I get it.

204
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:40,620
Huh?

205
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:41,990
Ah, well...

206
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:43,369
I'm not taking Natsuki's side.

207
00:08:43,370 --> 00:08:44,646
I'm taking the girlfriend's side.

208
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:46,649
Whenever I fall for someone,

209
00:08:46,650 --> 00:08:48,760
I'm the one who pursues them until we date.

210
00:08:49,610 --> 00:08:53,580
But they never seem to match my enthusiasm.

211
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,850
So it never lasts long.

212
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,240
Since Natsuki and I are total opposites,

213
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:01,230
sometimes seeing him
like that just frustrates me.

214
00:09:01,550 --> 00:09:05,230
I even got mad and told him, "You don't
understand how people in love feel at all."

215
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,846
I was just taking it out on him, wasn't I?

216
00:09:07,870 --> 00:09:09,020
Yeah, poor guy.

217
00:09:09,390 --> 00:09:10,390
Yeah.

218
00:09:10,890 --> 00:09:12,320
But I don't do that anymore lately.

219
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:15,470
Because now I pour all my love
into World Heritage Sites.

220
00:09:18,830 --> 00:09:20,360
But I think the current Natsuki

221
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:22,240
could probably understand you now.

222
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:27,000
Because he finally has the look
of someone who's truly in love.

223
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,760
Thanks for waiting. Here's
your sweet and sour pork.

224
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:39,500
Wait, Natsuki.

225
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,400
Is the yurinchi not good today?

226
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,800
No, it's delicious.

227
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,480
I've thought about it.

228
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:57,850
If I ever fell for a girl one day...

229
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:00,910
I'd probably still be at a loss.

230
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:06,960
But,

231
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,120
at the end of the day,

232
00:10:09,550 --> 00:10:10,910
what matters is the person, right?

233
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,210
It's not about gender.

234
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:18,220
It's about how you see that person.

235
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:22,680
Yeah...

236
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:23,990
Yeah.

237
00:10:25,370 --> 00:10:26,810
So I also hope

238
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:29,550
you can accept the real Natsuki.

239
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,710
I feel the same way.

240
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,140
But how should I put it...

241
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,829
I just feel like if I say the wrong thing,

242
00:10:38,830 --> 00:10:40,990
I might end up hurting Na-chan.

243
00:10:42,970 --> 00:10:45,650
I keep overthinking my words,
and end up not saying anything at all.

244
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:49,870
Maybe that's exactly
what's hurting him.

245
00:10:52,670 --> 00:10:54,190
So when you said "sorry" back then,

246
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:56,169
is that what you meant?

247
00:10:56,170 --> 00:10:56,720
Yeah.

248
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,760
I just didn't know how
to put it into words.

249
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:02,480
Ah... so that's it.

250
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:04,540
I see.

251
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,000
Thank goodness.

252
00:11:07,770 --> 00:11:08,770
Huh?

253
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,419
If your "sorry"

254
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,240
was meant to reject Natsuki's feelings,

255
00:11:13,770 --> 00:11:15,690
I probably would've
drop-kicked you on the spot.

256
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,839
Good thing it didn't come to that.

257
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:19,600
I'm just kidding.

258
00:11:19,601 --> 00:11:20,749
No, you seriously look like you'd do it.

259
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:22,239
I wouldn't kick you here.

260
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,789
What do you mean, "not here"?

261
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:25,136
Are you planning to kick me later?

262
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:27,479
Are you sure I can have such a nice melon?

263
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:29,049
Of course, please take it.

264
00:11:29,050 --> 00:11:31,500
A friend from my old band is farming now.

265
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,530
He sent over quite a few.

266
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:36,760
Then I'll gratefully accept it.

267
00:11:39,390 --> 00:11:40,280
Auntie.
Hmm?

268
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:43,609
Is Natsuki not back yet?

269
00:11:43,610 --> 00:11:44,430
Yeah.

270
00:11:44,431 --> 00:11:46,320
I think he's still at Kazuharu's place.

271
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:47,830
I see...

272
00:11:48,810 --> 00:11:51,630
Natsuki got dumped again, didn't he?

273
00:11:52,350 --> 00:11:53,350
Huh?

274
00:11:53,470 --> 00:11:54,560
Poor guy.

275
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:56,400
Riku.

276
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,280
Natsuki isn't pitiful at all.

277
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:01,150
Why not?

278
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:03,630
Sure, getting dumped hurts.

279
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:06,590
But isn't it also proof
that he truly cared for someone?

280
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,636
You know, when it comes to love,

281
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:11,400
even if it's just unrequited,

282
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:14,480
it still helps you grow.

283
00:12:16,270 --> 00:12:17,290
I don't get it.

284
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:19,570
Fair enough.

285
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,120
Honestly...

286
00:12:27,430 --> 00:12:30,260
(Seikosha Travel)

287
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,600
Huh?

288
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:32,960
Dad?

289
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:35,000
(Kusatsu Onsen Paradise)

290
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,630
Silver anniversary?

291
00:12:36,930 --> 00:12:37,930
Yeah.

292
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:41,780
We usually don't even
celebrate anniversaries,

293
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,210
sometimes I even forget them entirely.

294
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:46,286
So I figured we should at least
celebrate properly this time.

295
00:12:46,310 --> 00:12:47,490
I see...

296
00:12:48,070 --> 00:12:50,580
A surprise hot spring trip sounds awesome.

297
00:12:51,730 --> 00:12:53,140
Have you decided where to go?

298
00:12:53,830 --> 00:12:54,840
About that...

299
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:55,940
Fukuo...
I see.

300
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,160
Will that work?

301
00:12:58,161 --> 00:12:59,809
He said he knew a good inn,

302
00:12:59,810 --> 00:13:01,700
so I left it to him.

303
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,000
But that guy

304
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:04,950
actually got the dates wrong.

305
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,480
So I'm looking for one right now.

306
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:11,410
I see...
Makes sense.

307
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,160
But,

308
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,150
Dad, are you sure you'll be okay?

309
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:17,440
Hmm?

310
00:13:17,441 --> 00:13:19,281
Can you really keep it
a secret until the end?

311
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:21,169
Isn't that the whole point of a surprise?

312
00:13:21,170 --> 00:13:23,599
But isn't Mom already suspicious of you?

313
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,600
Ah...

314
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,580
Seriously, what should I do?

315
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:39,260
I'm home.

316
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:40,880
Ah.

317
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,850
Welcome back.

318
00:13:44,210 --> 00:13:45,030
I'm home.
Welcome back.

319
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,240
Uh, well...

320
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,160
We just bumped into each other outside.

321
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,240
I see...

322
00:13:52,710 --> 00:13:54,560
Natsuki, how was the mock exam?

323
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:55,980
Ah...

324
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:57,020
It was alright.

325
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,340
Rock.

326
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:00,290
I'm home.
- I see.
- Here.

327
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:03,650
I'm home.

328
00:14:03,651 --> 00:14:05,269
By the way, it's hot, isn't it?

329
00:14:05,270 --> 00:14:05,700
Yeah.

330
00:14:05,701 --> 00:14:06,869
Want to take a shower first?

331
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:07,250
Yeah.
I'll go take a shower.

332
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:08,480
Okay.

333
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:09,960
I'm going to take a shower.

334
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:13,680
Um, this is for you.

335
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:17,360
(Refreshing Mint Chocolate)
Well, Natsuki said he wanted some.

336
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,080
I see.

337
00:14:20,070 --> 00:14:21,750
I bought some for you too.

338
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,410
Thank you so much.

339
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,240
This is bad...

340
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:41,910
Oh, Rock.

341
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:43,840
You came over.

342
00:14:45,930 --> 00:14:48,930
Did you escape to my room because the
vibe between Mom and Dad is too awful?

343
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,360
Yeah.

344
00:14:58,760 --> 00:15:00,280
(New message from Kobayakawa Sota)
Huh?

345
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,570
How was the mock exam?

346
00:15:09,790 --> 00:15:12,719
(How was the mock exam?)

347
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:15,989
(I think it went pretty well.)

348
00:15:15,990 --> 00:15:17,139
(Read)
(I think it went pretty well.)

349
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:18,360
Wow, that was fast.

350
00:15:19,090 --> 00:15:20,090
That's great.

351
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,700
I can't wait for the results.

352
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:35,630
Hmm...

353
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:37,680
Is that it...?

354
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,200
Sigh...

355
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,900
Left on read...

356
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:44,540
Sigh...

357
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,349
I'll take this over then.

358
00:15:47,350 --> 00:15:48,369
Thanks for your help.

359
00:15:48,370 --> 00:15:49,459
Ah, thanks.

360
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:50,460
Okay.

361
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,800
Oh, Na-chan.

362
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:52,790
Hello.

363
00:15:52,791 --> 00:15:54,769
How long are you going to sleep?

364
00:15:54,770 --> 00:15:56,020
It's already noon.

365
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,929
I'm so lucky to see Na-chan's sleepy face.

366
00:15:58,930 --> 00:16:01,240
I couldn't really sleep last night.

367
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:04,559
Ah, Na-chan.

368
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:06,560
Could you say thanks to Sota-san for me?

369
00:16:07,410 --> 00:16:07,960
Huh?

370
00:16:07,961 --> 00:16:10,760
He came to our bakery
to buy bread yesterday.

371
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:13,110
I see.

372
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,999
Kaoru-san, you're jumping the gun.

373
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,249
What does it matter?

374
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:19,359
Well, I did tell him to come,

375
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:22,319
but I didn't expect him to actually
show up. It really surprised me.

376
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,649
He's really polite.

377
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:25,480
What did So-chan buy?

378
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:30,929
Tuna mayo toast, a
croissant, and salt bread.

379
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:31,930
Huh?

380
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:34,479
Aren't those all Natsuki's favorites?

381
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:35,840
Yeah, and he even asked me,

382
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:38,470
"What kind of bread does Na-chan like?"

383
00:16:54,230 --> 00:16:55,230
Delicious.

384
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:01,160
(Cloud Encyclopedia)

385
00:17:01,161 --> 00:17:04,400
Back then, I thought clouds were amazing.

386
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:08,640
It's about how you see that person.

387
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:13,840
So I also hope you can
accept the real Natsuki.

388
00:17:49,650 --> 00:17:50,650
Huh?

389
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Huh?

390
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,600
I was just about to go look for you.

391
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:18,880
I was looking for you, too.

392
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:20,920
Huh?

393
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:25,570
I wanted... to have a proper talk with you.

394
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,720
Me too.

395
00:18:33,810 --> 00:18:34,810
Um...

396
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:37,300
Yeah?

397
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,940
About what happened last time...

398
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:44,450
I meant it.

399
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,590
I'm sorry for putting you on the spot.

400
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:52,060
No.

401
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:54,220
You didn't do anything wrong, Na-chan.

402
00:18:55,250 --> 00:18:56,980
I'm the one who should be apologizing.

403
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:58,940
Huh?

404
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:01,300
Back then,

405
00:19:03,230 --> 00:19:04,860
I said "I'm sorry" to you.

406
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:07,590
I'm sorry.

407
00:19:07,890 --> 00:19:08,450
No, it's fine.

408
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:10,050
Um, it's really okay.

409
00:19:13,170 --> 00:19:14,780
I was actually really happy.

410
00:19:16,690 --> 00:19:17,120
Huh?

411
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,600
I mean, I was definitely caught off guard,

412
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,600
Yeah.

413
00:19:23,410 --> 00:19:24,410
But I was happy.

414
00:19:28,290 --> 00:19:29,290
But...

415
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:34,180
I didn't know if it was
okay to just say "I'm happy."

416
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:38,620
That's why I said "I'm sorry."

417
00:19:41,550 --> 00:19:43,810
I'm really... so sorry.

418
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:46,689
Ah, no.

419
00:19:46,690 --> 00:19:47,700
Um, well...

420
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:51,600
That "sorry" just now
was because I used the wrong words.

421
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:53,320
Um...

422
00:19:55,550 --> 00:19:57,920
It's just like my sister said.

423
00:19:58,750 --> 00:19:59,750
Huh?

424
00:20:01,230 --> 00:20:02,230
I...

425
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:05,969
I thought you'd find me disgusting.

426
00:20:05,970 --> 00:20:06,970
No.

427
00:20:07,070 --> 00:20:08,070
I'd never think that.

428
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:11,140
That's what my sister said, too.

429
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:14,800
She said, "Sota isn't like that."

430
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:18,860
I see.

431
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:20,620
Yeah.

432
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:25,380
You know...

433
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:26,840
Hmm?

434
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,450
The tuna toast and salt
bread are both delicious.

435
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:32,730
But...

436
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:35,300
Croissants aren't really my thing.

437
00:20:36,770 --> 00:20:37,250
Huh?

438
00:20:37,630 --> 00:20:38,630
Ah.

439
00:20:38,830 --> 00:20:40,436
What about sweet ones? Which do you like?

440
00:20:40,460 --> 00:20:41,580
Red bean? Chocolate?

441
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:43,460
Or something with whipped cream?

442
00:20:44,060 --> 00:20:45,979
Uh...

443
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:46,980
Or how about this?

444
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:48,820
What's your favorite rice ball filling?

445
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:50,920
Huh?

446
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,450
I want to know more about you.

447
00:20:53,630 --> 00:20:54,630
Ah...

448
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:56,030
You mean about food?

449
00:20:56,370 --> 00:20:57,370
No.

450
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,500
About everything.

451
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:03,360
I want to talk to you
about all sorts of things.

452
00:21:03,570 --> 00:21:05,700
About the sky, about bridges.

453
00:21:06,450 --> 00:21:07,490
About serious stuff.

454
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,040
And about trivial little things.

455
00:21:09,950 --> 00:21:11,110
I want to talk with you more.

456
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,330
And get to know you better.

457
00:21:17,410 --> 00:21:18,410
I...

458
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:24,450
I'm absolutely sure that I like you.

459
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:26,300
Huh?

460
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:27,590
But...

461
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:31,780
I still don't know what kind of "like"
it actually is.

462
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:35,790
Is it friendship?

463
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,600
Or like how I see a younger brother?

464
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:39,220
No.

465
00:21:39,490 --> 00:21:42,020
Is it admiration? Or is it love?

466
00:21:44,610 --> 00:21:47,470
It feels like all of them are right.

467
00:21:48,020 --> 00:21:51,020
But at the same time,
none of them feel quite right.

468
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:54,140
What do you think?

469
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:56,140
Huh?

470
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:57,620
Um...

471
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,010
I don't know either...

472
00:22:00,060 --> 00:22:01,060
I see.

473
00:22:02,190 --> 00:22:03,190
Makes sense.

474
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:05,460
But...

475
00:22:05,550 --> 00:22:07,379
I think if I just get to
know you a little better,

476
00:22:07,380 --> 00:22:09,220
I feel like I'll be able
to find the answer.

477
00:22:11,550 --> 00:22:12,550
So...

478
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:17,070
Will you search for the answer with me?

479
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:21,980
Yeah.

480
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:23,720
I want to search for it with you.

481
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:24,430
Really?

482
00:22:24,690 --> 00:22:27,170
I want to get to know Sota better, too.

483
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:30,670
Then let's talk a lot more.

484
00:22:31,860 --> 00:22:32,860
Yeah.

485
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:38,880
Even if the answer we find isn't "love,"
that's okay.

486
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:41,570
I'm home.

487
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:43,710
Huh, is Mom not here?

488
00:22:44,380 --> 00:22:45,980
Ah, Rock is here.

489
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,269
Good boy.

490
00:22:48,270 --> 00:22:50,479
You're so cute.

491
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,480
Good boy, you're so sweet.

492
00:22:55,700 --> 00:22:56,700
Huh?

493
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:01,019
(When My Son Falls in Love with a Man)

494
00:23:01,020 --> 00:23:03,069
Well, as for me...

495
00:23:03,070 --> 00:23:04,899
I prefer harder breads.

496
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:05,550
Huh?

497
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:07,059
Like baguettes, bagels, and stuff.

498
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:07,970
Seriously?
Yeah.

499
00:23:08,321 --> 00:23:10,159
Hard bread makes my
jaw tired, so I don't like it.

500
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:11,499
That's the best part.

501
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:12,160
No way.
Huh?

502
00:23:12,831 --> 00:23:15,019
- I still prefer the soft and fluffy ones.
- Because...

503
00:23:15,020 --> 00:23:18,209
This time right now
feels like a precious treasure to me.

504
00:23:18,210 --> 00:23:19,210
Ah.

505
00:23:19,490 --> 00:23:20,909
(This story is purely fictional.)
It's a contrail.

506
00:23:20,910 --> 00:23:21,550
(Next Episode)

507
00:23:21,551 --> 00:23:23,469
I want to go out and have fun with So-chan.

508
00:23:23,470 --> 00:23:25,520
(Endless Love, A Reward Date)
Na-chan.

509
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:29,059
I'm the only one who's excited.

510
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:30,179
Smile.

511
00:23:30,180 --> 00:23:32,350
Is Natsuki doing okay?

512
00:23:32,560 --> 00:23:34,259
(Love Brings Signs of a Storm)
You've already noticed, haven't you?

513
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:38,110
I can't tell you right now.
